title: fix(bridge-hub): expose try-runtime feature in bridge-hub-test-utils

doc:
  audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    Fixes #10962

    **Summary**  
    When running `cargo test --features try-runtime` (or `--all-features`) on BridgeHub runtimes, compilation failed with:

    ```
    error[E0046]: not all trait items implemented, missing: `try_successful_origin`
     --> .../assets-common-.../foreign_creators.rs:29:1
    ```

    Root cause: `bridge-hub-test-utils` lacked a `try-runtime` feature, preventing propagation to `asset-test-utils` → `assets-common`.  
    This caused `assets-common` to be compiled without `try-runtime` while `frame-support` had it enabled → missing `try_successful_origin` method (guarded by `#[cfg(feature = "try-runtime")]`).

    **Changes**  
    - Added `try-runtime` feature to `bridge-hub-test-utils/Cargo.toml`, forwarding only to the 16 crates that declare/support it.  
    - Activated the feature in the two test runtimes:  
      - `cumulus/parachains/runtimes/bridge-hubs/bridge-hub-rococo/Cargo.toml`  
      - `cumulus/parachains/runtimes/bridge-hubs/bridge-hub-westend/Cargo.toml`

    After these changes, `cargo check --features try-runtime` and  
    `SKIP_PALLET_REVIVE_FIXTURES=1 cargo test -p bridge-hub-*-runtime --release --locked -q --all-features`  
    pass cleanly on both rococo and westend runtimes.


crates:
  - name: bridge-hub-rococo-runtime
    bump: patch
  - name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
  - name: bridge-hub-test-utils
    bump: patch
